rything else names ","type":"text"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"this tenant’s","type":"text"}],"type":"emphasis"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"domains or ","type":"text"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"this tenant’s","type":"text"}],"type":"emphasis"},{"text":" bounds, and there is no sense in which one tenant’s list of","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"trusted publishers is stricter than another’s — the same argument [","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"OidcPolicy"},{"text":"] already","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"makes for ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"dcr_allowed_redirect_hosts"},{"text":". # Every bound here is a security control","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"[","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Self::max_metadata_bytes"},{"text":"], [","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Self::min_cache_secs"},{"text":"] and [","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Self::max_cache_secs"},{"text":"] are not","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"tuning knobs. They are, respectively, the ceiling on a read from an attacker-chosen URL, the","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"floor under how often that read may be repeated, and the ceiling on how long its result may","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"be trusted. Each is clamped again in code against the three constants above, so a settings","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"row written by hand cannot lift them.","type":"text"}],"fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"struct"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"CimdPolicy"}]},"doc://AxiamSDK/documentation/AxiamSDK/OidcPolicy":{"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"OpenID Connect surface controls (X7 G8, plan §4.6\/§4.8; T21.4). Settings that are not"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"password rules, here because this is the org-baseline-plus-tenant-override surface every"},{"type":